XQuartz: no App Nap, precise timers (the X server shows the games)

Wine's Mac driver holds an NSProcessInfo activity for the life of every
process (UserInitiatedAllowingIdleSystemSleep; CodeWeavers' sources,
dlls/winemac.drv/cocoa_app.m), so macOS never naps it. SteamARM-X11.app is
the application whose windows show every game and, with Game Mode, the
game macOS sees: the same activity, latency-critical too (timer and I/O
precision for input and presentation).

--- a/hw/xquartz/X11Application.m
+++ b/hw/xquartz/X11Application.m
@@ -797,6 +797,15 @@
         /* Tell the server thread that it can proceed */
         QuartzInitServer(argc, argv, envp);
 
+        /* SteamARM: never App Nap this server -- it shows the games -- and keep
+         * its timers precise, as Wine's Mac driver does for its processes
+         * (cocoa_app.m, beginActivityWithOptions). Held for the process's life. */
+        static id steamarm_activity;
+        steamarm_activity = [[[NSProcessInfo processInfo]
+            beginActivityWithOptions:(NSActivityUserInitiatedAllowingIdleSystemSleep |
+                                      NSActivityLatencyCritical)
+                              reason:@"X server for games"] retain];
+
         /* This must be done after QuartzInitServer because it can result in
          * an mieqEnqueue() - <rdar://problem/6300249>
          */
